---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Stitch from "../components/Stitch.astro";
import PillarCard from "../components/PillarCard.astro";
import ProjectCard from "../components/ProjectCard.astro";
import PullQuote from "../components/PullQuote.astro";
---

<Base
	title="Automate Ethically"
	description="A movement for automation with a human in the loop: laws that keep a person accountable for every automated decision, software built on that principle, and help retraining for durable work."
>
	<header class="ae-header">
		<a class="ae-wordmark" href="/">
			<span class="ae-wordmark-pill">automate&nbsp;ethically</span>
		</a>
		<nav class="ae-nav" aria-label="Sections">
			<a href="#organize">Organize</a>
			<a href="#build">Build</a>
			<a href="#retrain">Retrain</a>
			<a href="#get-involved">Get involved</a>
		</nav>
	</header>

	<main id="main">
		<!-- DRAFT: rewrite — copy task 1: hero headline + subhead -->
		<section class="ae-hero" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
			<p class="ae-eyebrow">A movement for ethical automation</p>
			<h1 id="hero-title">A human makes the decision.</h1>
			<p class="ae-hero-sub">
				Automation can act. Only a person can decide — and a person can be held
				accountable. We organize for laws, build software, and support workers
				on that one principle.
			</p>
			<figure class="ae-epigraph">
				<blockquote>
					The loom did not remove the weaver. A person still chose the pattern,
					punched the cards, examined the cloth, and signed the bolt.
				</blockquote>
				<figcaption>jacquard, 1804 — and the rule we intend to keep</figcaption>
			</figure>
			<div class="ae-cta-row">
				<a class="ae-btn ae-btn--primary" href="#get-involved">Get involved</a>
				<a class="ae-btn ae-btn--ghost" href="#manifesto">Read the manifesto</a>
			</div>
		</section>

		<Stitch />

		<!-- DRAFT: rewrite — copy task 2: manifesto -->
		<section class="ae-section" id="manifesto" aria-labelledby="manifesto-title">
			<div class="ae-container">
				<p class="ae-eyebrow">Why now</p>
				<h2 class="ae-h2" id="manifesto-title">
					The anger is real. Aim it at the rulebook.
				</h2>
				<div class="ae-prose">
					<p>
						People are angry at data centers. People are angry at license-plate
						cameras on every corner. The anger is not confusion. It is a correct
						reaction to automation and surveillance arriving without consent,
						without accountability, and without a plan for the people it
						displaces.
					</p>
					<p>
						But a data center is a totem. Tear one down and the automation it
						served moves elsewhere. The durable win is not obstruction. It is
						law: rules that require a human to make the decision, and to answer
						for it, wherever an automated system touches a person's life.
					</p>
					<p>
						Machines do not accept responsibility. Companies do not volunteer
						it. Rules that protect people change only when people organize —
						city by city, then state by state.
					</p>
				</div>
				<PullQuote attribution="Detlefs' Law">
					In an automation arms race, the automations favoring laziness will
					always outpace the automations favoring intellectual rigor.
				</PullQuote>
			</div>
		</section>

		<Stitch />

		<section class="ae-section ae-section--tint" aria-labelledby="pillars-title">
			<div class="ae-container">
				<p class="ae-eyebrow">The work</p>
				<h2 class="ae-h2" id="pillars-title">Three pillars, one principle</h2>
				<div class="ae-pillars">
					<!-- DRAFT: rewrite — copy task 3: pillar Organize -->
					<PillarCard title="Organize" chip="organizing now" id="organize">
						<p>
							Start where the decisions are made: city councils, county boards,
							school boards. Ask for one ordinance:
							<strong>an automation may act, but a person decides — and that
							person is accountable.</strong> Then carry it to the state house.
						</p>
					</PillarCard>
					<!-- DRAFT: rewrite — copy task 4: pillar Build ethically -->
					<PillarCard title="Build ethically" chip="software below" id="build">
						<p>
							Policy asks people to behave. Software can make the rule
							physical. We build tools where
							<strong>accountability is enforced by the build itself</strong> —
							a machine can propose, but it cannot sign.
						</p>
					</PillarCard>
					<!-- DRAFT: rewrite — copy task 5: pillar Retrain -->
					<PillarCard title="Retrain" chip="coming" chipQuiet id="retrain">
						<p>
							The honest answer to "there will always be more work" is a
							coordination layer that helps people
							<strong>learn the next field while they still have this
							job</strong> — from the office, from home, before the pink slip.
							Without that layer, optimism becomes cruelty.
						</p>
					</PillarCard>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<Stitch />

		<section class="ae-section" id="projects" aria-labelledby="projects-title">
			<div class="ae-container">
				<p class="ae-eyebrow">Built on these principles</p>
				<h2 class="ae-h2" id="projects-title">Proof, in working code</h2>
				<div class="ae-projects">
					<!-- DRAFT: rewrite — copy task 6: project card jacquard -->
					<ProjectCard name="jacquard" chip="in development" chipQuiet>
						<p>
							Version control where a decision is an object in the graph. An
							agent can draft a decision and propose it.
						</p>
						<p class="ae-project-human">
							Only a person can settle it — with a few sentences in their own
							words, under their own name.
						</p>
					</ProjectCard>
					<!-- DRAFT: rewrite — copy task 7: project card phantom-thread -->
					<ProjectCard name="phantom-thread" chip="request an invite">
						<p>
							A careful review and a rubber stamp leave the same green check.
							phantom-thread makes them distinguishable — and rewards the
							careful one.
						</p>
						<p>
							<a href="https://jdetle.com/phantom-thread">Preview at
							jdetle.com/phantom-thread</a> (invite-gated today).
						</p>
					</ProjectCard>
				</div>
				<p class="ae-aside">
					The thinking behind these tools lives at
					<a href="https://jdetle.com">jdetle.com</a>.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<Stitch />

		<!-- DRAFT: rewrite — copy task 8: movement / PAC-goal statement -->
		<section class="ae-section ae-section--tint" id="movement" aria-labelledby="movement-title">
			<div class="ae-container">
				<p class="ae-eyebrow">The movement</p>
				<h2 class="ae-h2" id="movement-title">Don't hate the player. Change the rulebook.</h2>
				<p class="ae-plain">
					We intend to form a registered political committee. Until that
					exists, we are neighbors, builders, and organizers — and we are not
					asking for money.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- DRAFT: rewrite — copy task 9: get-involved CTA -->
		<section class="ae-section" id="get-involved" aria-labelledby="cta-title">
			<div class="ae-container">
				<p class="ae-eyebrow">Get involved</p>
				<h2 class="ae-h2" id="cta-title">Start with one email</h2>
				<p class="ae-plain">
					Tell us your city and what you can do — an hour a month is enough.
				</p>
				<div class="ae-cta-row">
					<a
						class="ae-btn ae-btn--primary"
						href="mailto:join@automate-ethically.com?subject=Count%20me%20in"
					>join@automate-ethically.com</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<div class="ae-coda">
			<p>
				&ldquo;Physics was the easy part. Everyone still has to become
				different at the same time, and everyone has a reason to go
				last.&rdquo;
			</p>
		</div>
	</main>

	<footer class="ae-footer">
		<!-- DRAFT: rewrite — copy task 10: footer -->
		<div class="ae-footer-inner">
			<span>&copy; 2026 John Detlefs &middot; <a href="https://jdetle.com">jdetle.com</a></span>
			<span class="ae-footer-sign">&hellip;and signed the bolt.</span>
		</div>
	</footer>
</Base>
